# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nimbus Weather — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the blanks:  cp .env.example .env
#
# THIS FILE USED TO DEFINE FIVE KEYS TWICE, with different values. `DATABASE_URL`,
# `REDIS_URL`, `WEATHER_PROVIDER_API_KEY`, `WEATHER_PROVIDER_BASE_URL` and
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` appeared in a Docker block and again in a local block, so
# every parser took the LAST occurrence and the first five lines were dead text
# that still looked editable. Anyone who filled in their database URL on line 4
# was editing a value the app never read.
#
# There is now one canonical set, with local-development defaults. If you are
# running `docker compose up`, the service hostnames differ — the commented block
# at the bottom has them. Compose supplies its own `db` and `redis` hostnames on
# the `db`/`redis` network, so you do not need to change these to use it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── App ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
CORS_ORIGIN=*

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Change before deploying anywhere. Rotating it invalidates every session.
JWT_SECRET=change-me

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker: postgres://postgres:postgres@db:5432/nimbus
DATABASE_URL=postgres://nimbus:nimbus@localhost:5432/nimbus_weather

# ── Redis ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker: redis://redis:6379
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# ── Weather provider ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The only value here with a real key in it. Get one from
# https://home.openweathermap.org/api_keys — the free tier is enough, and the
# free tier's limits are the reason the UI reports a 5-day forecast and 3-hourly
# buckets rather than 7-day and hourly. See README §"Provider note".
# The `/data/2.5` PATH IS REQUIRED — the bare host 404s.
# Verified: `https://api.openweathermap.org/weather?...` -> 404 Not Found, while
# `https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?...` -> 200. Nothing in the code
# appends the path: `openWeather.ts` uses this value verbatim, and `env.ts` validates
# it only as "some URL", which a bare host satisfies.
#
# The failure is silent and total. A 404 makes `weather.service.ts` fall back to
# `buildWeatherBundle(...)` tagged `source: "sample"`, so every city on the planet
# renders a fully-populated dashboard of deterministic INVENTED numbers, and the
# only server-side signal is a `logger.warn`. The web client discloses it; the
# mobile client does not read `bundle.source` at all, so a mobile user sees
# fabricated weather with no labelling whatsoever.
WEATHER_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
WEATHER_PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5

# ── Rate limiting ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
RATE_LIMIT_MAX=120

# ── Mobile ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker/host machine: http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1
# The `/v1` suffix is required — the mobile client appends `/weather/bundle`.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/v1
